The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST)) {
    if (dep->flags & DWC3_EP_TRANSFER_STARTED) {
        dwc3_stop_active_transfer(dwc, dep->number, true);
        dep->flags = DWC3_EP_ENABLED;
    } else {
        u32 cur_uf;
        cur_uf = __dwc3_gadget_get_frame(dwc);
        __dwc3_gadget_start_isoc(dwc, dep, cur_uf);
        dep->flags &= ~DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST;
    }
```
Reason:
The simplification in the handling of ISO transfers did not properly manage the state of ongoing transfers when the `XferInProgress` event occurred. Specifically, it failed to account for the scenario where an active transfer was already in progress, leading to premature stopping of transfers and a subsequent performance degradation.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_BUSY) &&
    !(dep->flags & DWC3_EP_MISSED_ISOC)) {
    WARN_ON_ONCE(!dep->resource_index);
    ret = __dwc3_gadget_kick_transfer(dep, dep->resource_index);
}
```
Reason:
The fix reintroduces the handling of ongoing ISO transfers by checking if the endpoint is busy and if there were no missed isochronous transfers. This ensures that the transfer can be kicked off correctly without stopping it prematurely, thereby restoring the original performance of ISO transfers.

